From b3cbc0be56ab8684d37b535c89c4722b60259fdc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kaloyan Naumov <knaumov@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 17:24:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0008-b70-ple-int8-rowscale-pinned-table
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

L2 PLE n-gram table in INT8, symmetric, one float32 scale per row (Lumnus-own, NOT from wu1ff)

Purpose:  Keep OUR BF16 PLE n-gram table as INT8 in the XPU pinned slabs: 164 B/row (160 int8 + the row's fp32
          scale), 48.88 GiB pinned over 4 ranks instead of 95.37 GiB (BF16) — within +1.2 GiB of FP8 (0007) at 4x
          lower reconstruction error (rel-L2 0.66 % vs 2.66 %, measured 2026-09-28).
          The table comes from B70_PLE_INT8_PATH: a .safetensors whose `table` is U8 [>= org_vocab, 164], built by
          tools/build_int8_ple.py in github.com/Lumnus/b70-flash-next (format tag lumnus-ple-int8-rowscale/v1).
          This patch:
            * B70_PLE_INT8=1 selects B70PLEInt8RowPinnedEmbeddingMethod (uint8 weight [rows, dim+4]) and pinned
              storage on XPU; refuses with B70_PLE_FP8=1 or without B70_PLE_INT8_PATH;
            * splits STORAGE width from LOGICAL width in the pinned embedding: `_b70_storage_dim = weight.shape[1]`
              drives the Triton gather width, BLOCK_D, the prefetch buffer, the forward output and the lookup shape;
              `embedding_dim` stays 160 (for BF16/FP8 storage the two are equal, so those paths are unchanged);
            * loads by zero-copy mmap (0007's reader) straight into uint8 pinned slabs (one 12.22 GiB slab/rank),
              rows verbatim — the scale travels with its row through the gather, the ETP reduce (uint8 now also
              reduced as an int8 byte sum; one owner per row, so exact) and the output copy;
            * dequantises after the gather with standard elementwise ops: q = bytes[:160].view(int8) -> fp32,
              s = bytes[160:164].view(float32), (q * s) -> one rounding to the activation dtype;
            * refuses to start on: wrong format tag, dtype != U8, width != dim+4, too few rows, n-gram layout tensors
              that differ from the model's, any non-finite/negative scale in this rank's rows (full slab scan), or —
              when PLE_TABLE_PATH (the BF16 table) is set — a cross-check above B70_PLE_INT8_MAX_REL_ERR (default
              0.02; expected ~0.0066) on 4096 random rows (B70_PLE_INT8_CROSSCHECK=0 skips it).
          Default OFF: with B70_PLE_INT8 unset every code path is 0007's/0006's/wu1ff's (the storage-width split
          is value-identical for BF16/FP8).
Depends:  0002 (pinned slabs), 0006 (direct-pinned fill), 0007 (safetensors reader, _b70_copy_rows, layout check).
Base:     vLLM v0.30.0 (ced6857afa0ea7b2e3f0846a62e1394e90f15607) after 0001-0007, i.e. sha256
          5251494c662fbc1d403d1641be5f3b12783518b49bde5fa1bdaa009b4cdaee4e (B70-0007, rev 2).
          Result: sha256 8dafd95b5657d4a0e267b49be2496b492e0190c916f134ddcf9f63f506276b20 (B70-0008).
Origin:   Lumnus.
Method:   diff -u against the post-0007 file (identical to the image); CPU unit test of the
          real patched functions, XPU pieces stubbed.
Apply:    patch -p1 --fuzz=0 from the directory that CONTAINS vllm/ (site-packages AND /workspace/vllm), after 0007.
